From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: vc1: fail the job when the header skip times out

The picture header skip ignores the bit reader timeout: with a stuck
bitstream engine every 24-bit step waits 1 ms, and the picture is then
decoded from a wrong position.

Fail the job on the first timeout.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
@@ -678,7 +678,12 @@
 			     VE_DEC_VC1_TRIGGER_TYPE_GET_BITS |
 			     VE_DEC_VC1_TRIGGER_TYPE_N_BITS(bits));
 
-		cedrus_wait_for(dev, VE_DEC_VC1_STATUS, VE_DEC_VC1_STATUS_BITS_BUSY);
+		if (cedrus_wait_for(dev, VE_DEC_VC1_STATUS,
+				    VE_DEC_VC1_STATUS_BITS_BUSY)) {
+			dev_err_ratelimited(dev->dev,
+					    "timed out waiting to skip bits\n");
+			return -ETIMEDOUT;
+		}
 	}
 
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_VC1_ROT_CTRL, 0);
